        {
          "id": 419328470,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I added unit tests based off the test for the ```fragment_add_seq()``` functions. The unit tests ```test_fragment_add_partial_reassembly```, ```test_fragment_add_duplicate_middle```, and ```test_fragment_add_duplicate_conflict``` pass with the change but do not pass in the current code, which doesn't set FD_OVERLAP and FD_OVERLAPCONFLICT as appropriate.\n\nThe tests ```test_fragment_add_duplicate_first``` and ```test_fragment_add_duplicate_last``` are a little odd because they test the current code, which throws exceptions instead of setting FD_OVERLAP _et al._ when new fragments are added after the reassembly is done (and partial reassembly isn't set.) I'm not sure that's the ultimate intended behavior, but I haven't looked at changing that yet. I altered those tests to catch the exception.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
